id: pm-rrwh2o
title: "Combining an annotation or linked-artifact mutation with a universal output control is refused untyped: code command_failed and pm --help examples instead of a stable code and a retry without the control"
description: "Found 2026-11-08 while verifying PR 1685 review findings. validateReadOutputOptions (src/sdk/read-output-contracts.ts) refuses a comments, notes, learnings, files, docs or package-catalog mutation combined with a universal output control (--output-budget, --output-cursor, --output-limit, --output-include, --output-session) with the message \"Universal output controls cannot be combined with a <command> mutation.\" The refusal carries no typed code. pm learnings <id> --add x --output-cursor bad --json reports code command_failed, required \"Adjust command input or tracker state and retry.\" and examples \"pm --help\" and \"pm <command> --help\". So an agent cannot key its recovery on the refusal, and the guidance never says what to do: run the mutation without the output control, or read with the output control after the write. Measured on the PR 1685 head with the built CLI in a sandbox tracker. Expected: a stable code (for example read_output_mutation_conflict), the offending output flags, and a suggested retry without them, through CLI, SDK and MCP. The refusal-closure census should count the new code. Duplicate check: searched universal output controls mutation refusal code. pm-479ggz (closed) rejected the controls for package manage diagnostics, and pm-f05lsg (open) measures recovery closure in general. Neither types this refusal."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[4]: agent-ux,read-output,recovery,refusals
created_at: "2026-11-08T01:16:13.804Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-08T17:01:49.580Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-08T13:44:55.153Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-08T13:44:55.153Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: "The mutation and output-control refusal carries a stable typed code that the error catalog and refusal-closure census include; The refusal names the offending output flags and suggests a retry of the mutation without them through CLI, SDK and MCP"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: low
repro_steps: "In a sandbox tracker run pm learnings <id> --add x --output-cursor bad --json and read the code, required and examples fields"
resolution: "validateReadOutputOptions throws read_output_mutation_conflict, exit 2, catalogued and listed in the refusal-closure census. It carries details.output_controls (the CLI flags), details.output_option_keys (the keys an SDK or MCP caller supplied), details.mutation_options, a required line and runnable per-surface examples. src/cli/runtime/read-output-mutation-retry.ts rewrites the CLI recovery as the caller's argv without each control and the value it consumed. Arity comes from scanOptionTokens in projection-retry.ts, and namespaced command paths resolve. The repair binds an environment-selected tracker like the other mutation retries. READ_OUTPUT_MUTATION_CONFLICT_CODE and READ_OUTPUT_SHAPING_CONTROL_FLAGS are exported."
expected_result: "The refusal carries a stable typed code, names the offending output flags, and suggests a retry of the mutation without them through CLI, SDK and MCP"
actual_result: "pm learnings <id> --add x --output-limit 3 --json exits 2 with code read_output_mutation_conflict, details.output_controls [--output-limit] and suggested_retry_args without the control; the retry runs; MCP tools/call returns the code with output_option_keys"
