comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-08T13:07:48.603Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation evidence, branch fix/annotation-read-fidelity. validateReadOutputOptions now throws readOutputMutationConflict. Fields: code read_output_mutation_conflict (exit 2, catalogued in generated-error-code-catalog-part-2.ts and listed in docs/generated/REFUSAL_CLOSURE_CENSUS.md); field (the first control); details.surface; details.output_controls (CLI flags); details.output_option_keys (the camelCase or snake_case keys the SDK or MCP caller supplied); details.mutation_options; a required line that says to retry without the controls and read with them separately; and runnable per-surface examples. HYBRID_READ_MUTATION_KEYS is now typed over exactly the six hybrid surfaces, so every surface has examples and no unreachable fallback exists. CLI: src/cli/runtime/read-output-mutation-retry.ts rewrites the recovery as the caller's argv without each control token and the value it consumed. It is wired into repairInvocationRecovery in main.ts beside the other mutation retries and binds an environment-selected tracker the same way. Flag arity comes from scanOptionTokens in projection-retry.ts, which now reports each token's consumed value, so arity has one source. The error path records argv as 'item comments ...', so the repair resolves the two-token command path before scanning. Verified with the built CLI: 'pm learnings <id> --add x --output-limit 3 --output-cursor=abc --output-row-contract --json' exits 2 with suggested_retry 'pm item learnings <id> --add x --json', and that retry runs. MCP tools/call returns the code, details and output_option_keys."
  "2026-11-08T14:21:01.481Z","harness:claude-code","Review fix on PR 1688 (Codex P1 and Greptile P2). The retry scanner reads value arity from vocabulary rows, which leave command flags such as --message untyped. Global normalization also lets a value-taking control swallow the next option: in 'comments pm-one --add kept --message --output-limit --pm-path /tmp/A --output-budget 500', --output-limit takes --pm-path as its value and the tracker path becomes the --message text. The rebuilt retry 'comments pm-one --add kept --message /tmp/A' was faithful to that parse, but it replayed the misparse as a clean write to the environment tracker. repairReadOutputMutationRecovery now withholds the retry in two cases. First, when a control consumed a flag-like token. Second, when a control directly follows a value-taking option, using the arity from enrichCliFlagInvocationContracts, which the flag-invocation parity gate verifies against the parser. In both cases the refusal still names the controls to drop. Specs cover the Codex argv, the dash-led budget case, the Greptile argv, '--add --output-limit', inline and boolean predecessors, a control before the command and a trailing control. A two-tracker CLI regression asserts that no retry is suggested and nothing is written. Measured on the built CLI: '--message --foo-bar' stores the message '--foo-bar', while '--message --pm-path X' and '--message --output-limit 2' are refused as an argument missing before any read-output refusal."
  "2026-11-08T14:41:08.769Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review of PR 1688, two findings declined with reasons. (1) The direct SDK runComments write with outputInclude in its global options: direct SDK primitives never apply universal output controls. A direct runComments read with outputLimit 1 still returns three rows. Shaping is a delivery-layer contract of the CLI and runAction, and runAction (the SDK and MCP transport) refuses the combination with read_output_mutation_conflict. Refusing direct writes would make writes stricter than reads at the same layer. (2) 'pm files discover <id> --apply --output-limit 3' gets the typed refusal but no suggested retry, because no contract source declares --apply: pm contracts --command 'files discover' is unknown_command. Withholding is the designed safe outcome. The contract gap is filed as pm-9ke7h9. A third finding, projection-retry arity for the search-advanced package's --for, concerns the pre-existing projection retry; this PR only moved that scanner, and an ambiguous argv already withholds the retry there."
  "2026-11-08T16:07:54.346Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit re-review of PR 1688 (Major), fixed. The retry is rebuilt from argv, but an embedded CLI run (PmClient-style, in-process) can execute inside an enclosing SDK withExpectedItemRevisions scope whose guards never reached argv. Run on its own, the retry would write unguarded. src/sdk/lifecycle/item-revision.ts gains isTrackerRevisionGuarded(pmRoot), true when activeItemRevisionExpectations reports guards or unreplayable nested ones. main.ts passes it lazily to repairReadOutputMutationRecovery, so it is evaluated only for this refusal code, and an active guard withholds the retry. Carrying the guards as --expect-hash tokens was not chosen: package-catalog mutations do not accept --expect-hash, and withholding is the safe outcome the refusal already explains. The control-token scan moved into controlTokenIndexes to keep complexity within the cap. docs/READ_OUTPUT_CONTRACTS.md now lists every case in which suggested_retry_args is withheld. Specs: the in-process CLI inside a real revision scope gets no retry, the same argv outside one does, and isTrackerRevisionGuarded covers outer and conflicting nested scopes. The per-surface examples are asserted exactly."
  "2026-11-08T17:01:49.579Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit round 4 on PR 1688. Fixed (Major): an argv carrying URL userinfo, such as a credentialed package source passed to 'package --catalog --install', now gets no executable retry, so the recovery never repeats the secret in another field. The pre-existing verbatim echo in attempted_command and normalized_args, which every refusal shares, is filed as pm-nhauur. Also fixed: the shared catalog recovery line now reads 'Inspect the structured error guidance, then retry the suggested command when one is present', since a withheld retry has no suggested command. The specs cover the credentialed and plain package sources and check the explicit tracker byte for byte in the two-tracker regression."
